    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Problem**: `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked correctly.\n\n**Root Cause**: The `--ci` flag is defined at the main frai CLI program level. When running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` option at the program level, so it wasn't being passed through in the `args` array to the gate subcommand's action handler.\n\n**Solution**: Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` in the `gate` command's action handler to:\n1. Check `process.argv` for the `gate` command\n2. Extract arguments that come after `gate` \n3. Look for `--ci` and `--scan` flags\n4. Append these flags to the arguments passed to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Verification**: \n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 `frai gate init` (without `--ci`) correctly skips creating the workflow file\n- \u2705 Package rebuilt successfully with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
